From 0e049d2fceb4f1846fd492c739086e2bf5c67d77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: charlotte bring-up <bringup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 01:57:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] ufs: charlotte: negotiate HS-G4 through the private
 UniPro window

The controller never completes standard UIC commands, so every
ufshcd_dme_get()/ufshcd_dme_set() used to time out.  That made
ufshcd_get_max_pwr_mode() fail, left hba->max_pwr_info invalid and the
link stuck in PWM-G1, which capped throughput at ~0.6 MB/s (PWM-G1 is
roughly 3 Mbit/s).

Route local DME accesses through the variant's private UniPro window and
supply the negotiated link parameters directly (the connected-lane and
gear attributes live on the peer, whose DME path is also broken here):

 - vops dme_get/dme_set: translate the core's (mib << 16) | selector
   encoding to the window's (selector << 16) | mib layout.
 - vops get_max_pwr_mode: report HS-G4, 2 lanes, rate B, matching the
   vendor DT (hufs-use-HS-GEAR4 / hufs-use-two-line).
 - After a successful PA_PWRMODE change re-apply the post-link PA layer
   knobs (PA_TActivate, PA_GRANULARITY) for the new gear.

Result on the QHW-100 (O_DIRECT, same micro-benchmark as 5.10):

  read 1 GiB bs=1M      987 MB/s (5.10)  ->  931 MB/s
  write 1 MiB bs=1M     598 MB/s         ->  726 MB/s
  read 4 KiB single     0.056 ms         ->  0.116 ms

Signed-off-by: charlotte bring-up <bringup@localhost>
